 oning at prime viewing locations for capturing striking photographs &amp\;
  securing a truly memorable occasion. Your experienced guide will navigate
  picturesque coastal thoroughfares and Newport's charming bridge view neig
 hborhoods\, making stops at both lesser-known vantage points &amp\; renown
 ed landmarks celebrated for their exceptional 'golden hour' illumination &
 amp\; sweeping ocean panoramas. 7:00 PM Tour (75 minutes) $150 per person 
 Available: Daily\, May 1 - December 31\, 2026 (Unavailable May 23 and May 
 31)\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/coastal-cruisers-the
 -golden-hour/109827/
LOCATION:Coastal Cruisers\, 478 Thames Street\, Newport\, RI 02840
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/coastal-cruisers-the-golden-hou
 r/109827/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack-O-Lantern Spectacular
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTSTAMP:20261021T153430Z
UID:ddc52d2e1f830141a3c1c36cbc2b@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Jack-O-Lantern Spectacular: The Great Pun-Kin Trail\, presente
 d by Citizens\, returns October 1 &#8211\; November 1 with an all-new trai
 l of clever carvings guaranteed to make you smile\, groan\, and laugh out 
 loud. This year’s theme celebrates the art of the pun\, with thousands o
 f hand-carved pumpkins bringing witty wordplay to life through pop culture
  references\, playful characters and pun-believable scenes. From clever on
 e-liners to delightfully cheesy dad jokes\, there’s something to make ev
 ery guest grin as they stroll The Great Pun-Kin Trail\, where over 5\,000 
 glowing jack-o’-lanterns illuminate the Zoo. Don’t miss New England’
 s “must-see” family-friendly event of the Halloween season at Roger Wi
 lliams Park Zoo. All tickets must be purchased online in advance. Tickets 
 are required and sold online only. No refunds or rescheduling. Buy Tickets
 \n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/jack-o-lantern-spectacu
 lar/92071/
LOCATION:Roger Williams Park Zoo\, 1000 Elmwood Avenue\, Providence\, RI 0
 2907
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/jack-o-lantern-spectacular/9207
 1/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Watercolor Series with Artist Mary Ellen Dwyer
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261119
DTSTAMP:20261021T153430Z
UID:25a45931f23d5e6972a9ca15cc1d@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Fall Watercolor Series with Artist Mary Ellen Dwyer Wednesdays
  | October 14 &#8211\; November 18 10:00 AM &#8211\; 12:00 PM Location: Ed
 ucation Room in Visitor’s Center Discover the joy of watercolor painting
  in this beginner/intermediate six-class series. Through demonstrations\, 
 learn the basics of watercolor tools\, color\, composition\, and paint app
 lications as you learn new techniques and work on developing your inner ta
 lent. Individualized instruction will guide each student in creating beaut
 iful watercolor paintings. Materials not included. See list of suggested m
 aterials below. Mary Ellen is a Signature artist of the RI Watercolor Soci
 ety and has been teaching for many years. Maximum of 10 students. Material
 s not included. These classes are for adults. Pre-registration is required
 . $210 Members | $250 Non-Members Register Here Suggested Supply List for 
 Watercolor Class If you have painted before\, please bring what you have. 
 Those supplies in boldface are essential for starting out: #2 Pencil or so
 fter (B) Sketchbook (any size) Kneaded eraser Brushes: sable or synthetic 
 or a combination of both: 1” flat\, ½” flat and #2 and #6 round Paint
 : Alizarin crimson\, cadmium yellow\, cobalt blue\, cadmium red\, French u
 ltramarine blue\, sap green\, viridian\, cerulean blue\, burnt sienna\, Pa
 yne’s gray\, raw umber\, raw sienna\, Naples yellow (or yellow ochre)\, 
 permanent rose\, new gamboge or lemon yellow. Palette: Mijello Fusion Pale
 tte or palette with large center for mixing (John Pike suggested)\, but an
 y will do such as inexpensive plastic palettes from craft or art stores. 1
 40lb cold press paper (good paper is essential!) Suggest “Arches” pape
 r: single sheets to be cut to size or any size watercolor block of paper (
 suggested). The Canson 9×12”\, 140 lb. watercolor pad is also acceptabl
 e for beginners. Support: which can be any lightweight board on which to t
 ape or clip paper (Masonite\, MDF board\, Styrofoam\, etc) and masking tap
 e or bull clips. A support is necessary only if you buy sheets of watercol
 or paper but not necessary if you buy a watercolor block.) Blocks come in 
 various sizes and are very convenient. Any size to start. Paper towels Pla
 stic container for water (such as recycled from take-out\, cottage cheese
 \, etc.) Other non-essential supplies: Natural sponge\, spray bottle for w
 ater\, masking fluid\, ruler\, white gouache. The use of these will be dem
 onstrated. If you have questions please do not hesitate to contact me at d
 wyermaryellen@gmail.com Good sources: Jerry’s Artarama or Blick/Urecht i
 n Providence or online\; Cheap Joe’s Art Stuff (online) or your local ar
 t supply shop. (Riverside Art in Somerset. Some of the supplies may be ava
 ilable at AC Moore\, Michael’s or Hobby Lobby.)\n\nSource: https://www.v
 isitrhodeisland.com/event/fall-watercolor-series-with-artist-mary-ellen-dw
 yer/111927/
LOCATION:Education Room in Visitor’s Center Discover the joy of watercol
 or painting in this beginner/intermediate six-class series. Through demons
 trations\, learn the basics of watercolor tools\, color\, composition\, an
 d paint applications as you learn new techniques and work on developing yo
 ur inner talent. Individualized instruction will guide each student in cre
 ating beautiful watercolor paintings. Materials not included. See list of 
 suggested materials below. Mary Ellen is a Signature artist of the RI Wate
 rcolor Society and has been teaching for many years. Maximum of 10 student
 s. Materials not included. These classes are for adults. Pre-registration 
 is required. $210 Members | $250 Non-Members Register Here Suggested Suppl
 y List for Watercolor Class If you have painted before\, please bring what
  you have. Those supplies in boldface are essential for starting out: #2 P
 encil or softer (B) Sketchbook (any size) Kneaded eraser Brushes: sable or
  synthetic or a combination of both: 1” flat\, ½” flat and #2 and #6 
 round Paint: Alizarin crimson\, cadmium yellow\, cobalt blue \, cadmium re
 d\, French ultramarine blue\, sap green\, viridian\, cerulean blue\, burnt
  sienna\, Payne’s gray\, raw umber\, raw sienna\, Naples yellow (or yell
 ow ochre)\, permanent rose\, new gamboge or lemon yellow. Palette: Mijello
  Fusion Palette or palette with large center for mixing (John Pike suggest
 ed)\, but any will do such as inexpensive plastic palettes from craft or a
 rt stores. 140lb cold press paper (good paper is essential!) Suggest “Ar
 ches” paper: single sheets to be cut to size or any size watercolor bloc
 k of paper (suggested). The Canson 9×12”\, 140 lb. watercolor pad is al
 so acceptable for beginners. Support: which can be any lightweight board o
 n which to tape or clip paper (Masonite\, MDF board\, Styrofoam\, etc) and
  masking tape or bull clips. A support is necessary only if you buy sheets
  of watercolor paper but not necessary if you buy a watercolor block.) Blo
 cks come in various sizes and are very convenient. Any size to start. Pape
 r towels Plastic container for water (such as recycled from take-out\, cot
 tage cheese\, etc.) Other non-essential supplies: Natural sponge\, spray b
 ottle for water\, masking fluid\, ruler\, white gouache. The use of these 
 will be demonstrated. If you have questions please do not hesitate to cont
 act me at dwyermaryellen@gmail.com Good sources: Jerry’s Artarama or Bli
 ck/Urecht in Providence or online\; Cheap Joe’s Art Stuff (online) or yo
 ur local art supply shop. (Riverside Art in Somerset. Some of the supplies
  may be available at AC Moore\, Michael’s or Hobby Lobby.) Show More Vie
 w Website | Email 1 / 1 Additional Information\, 101 Ferry Road\, Bristol
 \, RI 02809
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/fall-watercolor-series-with-art
 ist-mary-ellen-dwyer/111927/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A New England Thanksgiving
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTSTAMP:20261021T153430Z
UID:21d35714802ba10832a84ed3bbac@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Join the Coggeshall staff as we prepare a Thanksgiving meal ov
 er the hearth in our historic farmhouse. The late 18th century was before 
 the official start of Thanksgiving as a national holiday\, but the day was
  still celebrated with food and prayer in New England. Watch our costumed 
 historians make chicken on a string\, bake a pie in the hot coals\, mash t
 urnips and churn butter. In the woodshop we will also demonstrate carving 
 wooden spoons. Explore the garden to see the last of the fall harvest. Wal
 k the nature trail and look for signs of wild turkey\, see musket demonstr
 ations and try your aim with rubber band targets. Please note: This is not
  a Thanksgiving meal for visitors to eat. Food prepared in the historic Fa
 rmhouse Kitchen does not meet modern health and food preparation codes for
  public consumption.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-n
 ew-england-thanksgiving/112116/
LOCATION:Coggeshall Farm Museum\, 1 Colt Drive\, Bristol\, 02809 Time: 10:
 00 AM to 4:00 PM
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-new-england-thanksgiving/1121
 16/
END:VEVENT
